plouðsion ejn twðé puriú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0367" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0367D"></COL> Ms.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katakekrumevnon</FOREIGN> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katakekrimevnon hJ ajlhvqeia levgei, tivû sofoúû, oåstiû twðn ajpodedokimasmevnwn taúû yucaúû ejn twðé
puriú krateiðsqai ajrnhvshtai_</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0367"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>PETR. 1Idouú thðé ajpologivaé tauvthé kaiú thðé marturivaé eijû
pivstwsin klivnetai hJ yuchú,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0367" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0367D"></COL> Ms.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajllaú ajfeqeiðsa . . . . uJpestrevfei</FOREIGN> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajllaú peraioumevnh pavlin eijû
yucrovthta ejpistrevfei. Pwðû gaúr ajswvmaton praðgma,
paraú swmatikouð eiædouû krathqhðnai kaiú blhqhðnai duvnatai,
ajgnowð.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0367"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>GRHGOR. Eijpeú, aijtwð se, kaiú ajpostatikaú pneuvmata,
taú ejk thðû oujranivou dovxhû ejkrifevnta, swmatikaú uJpavrcein,
hÞ ajswvmata uJpolambavneiû_</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0367"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>PETR. Tivû uJgihð</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0367" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0367D"></COL> Ms.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJgihvû</FOREIGN> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>logizovmenoû, swmatikaú uJpavrcein
taú pneuvmata levxhé_</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0367"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>GRHGOR. Toú deú geevnnhû puðr ajswvmaton uJpavrcein levgeiû,
hÞ swmatikovn_</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0367"><COL N="0367C"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>PETR. Toú deú geevnnhû puðr swmatikoún uJpavrcein oujk ajmfibavllw,
ejn wßé swvmata ejn pavshé ajlhqeivaé kriqhvsontai.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0367"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>GRHGOR. Toiðû katadivkoiû hJ oæntwû ajlhvqeia Cristoúû oJ
Qeoúû hJmwðn ejn thðé sunteleivaé ejreið× 2Upavgete eijû toú puðr toú
aijwvnion toú hJtoimasmevnon twðé diabovlwé kaiú toiðû ajggevloiû
aujtouð. 1Eaún ouøn oJ diavboloû kaiú oiJ aæggeloi aujtouð ajswvmatoi
oænteû, twðé swmatikwðé puriú kriqhðnai mevllousi, tiv qaumastoún
ejaún kaiú aiJ yucaiú proú touð ajpolabeiðn taú swvmata,
swmatikwðn</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0367" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0367D"></COL> Ms.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>basavnwn</FOREIGN> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>krithrivwn duvnantai aijsqavnesqai_</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0367"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>PETR. Faneraðû ouæshû thðû ajpologivaû, oujk ojfeivlei touð
loipouð hJ yuchú periú tauvthû thðû ejkzhthvsewû distavsai.</FOREIGN></P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0367" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0367">CAPUT XXX.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">De morte Theodorici regis Ariani.</HI></HEAD> <COL N="0368C"></COL> <P COM="0368">GREGORIUS. Postquam laboriose credidisti, operae
pretium credo, si ea quae mihi a viris fidelibus sunt
 <COL N="0368D"></COL> digesta narravero. <NOTE N="i" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0368" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0368D"></COL> Hic incipit cap. in Gemet.</NOTE>  Julianus namque hujus Romanae
Ecclesiae, cui Deo auctore deservio, secundus defensor,
qui ante septem ferme annos defunctus est,
ad me adhuc in monasterio positum crebro veniebat,
et mecum colloqui de animae utilitate consueverat.
 <COL N="0369A"></COL> Hic itaque mihi quadam die narravit,  <HI REND=BOLD>420</HI>  dicens:
 <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0369" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0369C"></COL> Regis Gothorum in Italia de quo fusissime egimus
in Vita Cassiodori, potissimum l. I, c. 3, usque
 <COL N="0369D"></COL> ad 6 inclusive. Consule etiam Paul. Diac. Hist. Miscell.
l. XV, et Greg. Turon. de Gloria Mart., c. 40. Olim
notus erat quidam locus qui  <HI REND="ITALIC">Theodorici in fernus</HI>  dicebatur.
Vide Act. SS. Ord. S. Ben. saecul. III, part. II,
pag. 379.</NOTE>  Theodorici regis temporibus pater soceri mei in
Sicilia <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0369" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0369D"></COL> Qui hoc munere fungebantur dicebantur  <HI REND="ITALIC">canonicarii,</HI> 
ut videre est apud Cassiod., max. l. VI Var.,
form. 8, et l. XII, c. 13. Non solum frumentum, sed
etiam pecuniam exigebant; hinc apud eumdem
Cassiod.  <HI REND="ITALIC">canonici solidi,</HI>  l. II, Var., ep. 25. Lege
etiam Sidon. Apoll. ep. 10 I. VI et notas doct. Savaronis.</NOTE>  exactionem canonis egerat, atque jam ad
Italiam redibat. Cujus navis appulsa est ad insulam
quae Liparis appellatur. Et quia illic vir quidam solitarius
magnae virtutis habitabat, dum nautae navis
armamenta repararent, visum est praedicto patri soceri
mei ad eumdem virum Dei pergere, seque ejus
orationibus commendare. Quos vir Domini cum vidisset,
eis inter alia colloquens, dixit: Scitis quia
rex Theodoricus mortuus est? Cui illi protinus responderunt:
Absit, nos eum viventem dimisimus, et nihil
tale ad nos de eo nuncusque perlatum est. Quibus
Dei famulus addidit, dicens: Etiam mortuus est: nam
hesterno die hora nona <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0369" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0369D"></COL> Is fuit Joannes I, qui Hormisdae successit an. 523.</NOTE>  inter Joannem papam et
 <COL N="0369B"></COL> Symmachum patricium discinctus atque discalceatus
et vinctis manibus deductus, in hanc vicinam Vulcani
 <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0369" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0369D"></COL> In nonnullis Mss. Norm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">insulam;</HI>  quae lectio
confirmatur ex Vers. Graeca.</NOTE>  ollam jactatus est. Quod illi audientes, sollicite
conscripserunt diem, atque in Italiam reversi, eo die
Theodoricum regem invenerunt fuisse mortuum quo
ejus exitus atque supplicium Dei famulo fuerat ostensum.
Et quia Joannem papam affligendo in custodia
occidit, Symmachum quoque patricium ferro trucidavit,
ab illis juste in ignem missus apparuit, quos in hac
vita injuste judicavit.</P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0369" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0369"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>KEFAL. LA'.
1Erwvthsiû, eij metaú qavnaton kaqartikoún puðr uJpavrcei.</FOREIGN></HEAD> <COL N="0367C"></COL> <P COM="0367"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>GRHGORIOS. 2Hnivka metaú kamavtou ejpivsteusaû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0367" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0367D"></COL> Ms.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thðé ejrgasivaé</FOREIGN> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thðû
